meta {
  name: Point at the order server
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{spenser}}/setSettings?serverUrl={{deviceFhirBase}}&orderMode=both&pollEnabled=1&pollSeconds=30&writeBack=1&giveUpOnStockEmpty=0
  body: none
  auth: none
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.orderMode: eq both
  res.body.giveUpOnStockEmpty: eq false
}

docs {
  orderMode=both is the default and what every scenario here assumes: a tag
  and a Task are two ways of authorizing the same dispense, so the unit
  checks for both on every poll. When an order arrives by both routes at
  once the Task wins, and the order is still dispensed only once.

  Note deviceFhirBase, not fhirBase: the deployment publishes the order
  server on both schemes, and Caddyfile.spenser keeps the plain-http site
  precisely so the device can reach it. The firmware does handle https://
  as well (certificates are not validated), so fhirBase works too - http
  just saves the ESP32 a TLS handshake on every poll.
}
